{"from": "text:2-kings-1-2-baal-zebub", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-10-25-beelzebul", "note": "Cross-reference: 2 Kings 1:2 names Baal-zebub, 'the god of Ekron', the biblical name behind 'Beelzebul' on the modern etymologies recorded on the claim; a biblical text is not independent evidence."}
{"from": "text:genesis-19-24", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-10-15-sodom-gomorrah-judgment", "note": "Cross-reference: Genesis 19:24 narrates the destruction ('Yahweh rained on Sodom and on Gomorrah sulfur and fire'), the memory Matt 10:15 invokes; a biblical text is not independent evidence."}
{"from": "person:thaddaeus", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-10-02-04-names-of-the-twelve", "note": "Identity dispute: the WEB text of Matt 10:3 reads 'Lebbaeus, who was also called Thaddaeus'; the fetched Jude the Apostle article states Thaddeus is 'generally identified' with Judas son of James and 'variously called ... Lebbaeus', so the identity of the tenth name is a modern reconciliation, not a settled fact."}
